## Strict TypeScript Rules

### Type Safety (CRITICAL)
- ✅ `strict: true` in tsconfig.json
- ✅ NO `any` types - EVER
- ✅ Explicit return types for all functions
- ✅ Readonly where possible
- ✅ Proper null/undefined handling

### Example - GOOD:
```typescript
/**
 * Process user query with AI
 * @param query User's search query
 * @returns Promise with search intent
 */
export async function processQuery(query: string): Promise<SearchIntent> {
  if (!query.trim()) {
    throw new Error('Query cannot be empty');
  }
  // implementation
}
```

### Example - BAD:
```typescript
// ❌ No JSDoc
// ❌ No explicit return type
// ❌ No validation
async function processQuery(query) {
  return await doSomething(query);
}
```

## Naming Conventions (MANDATORY)

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT
const userName = "John";                    // camelCase for variables
const MAX_RETRIES = 3;                      // SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE for constants
class UserService {}                        // PascalCase for classes
function calculateTotal() {}                // camelCase for functions
interface SearchQuery {}                    // PascalCase for interfaces
type AIProvider = 'claude' | 'openai';     // PascalCase for types

// ❌ WRONG
const UserName = "John";                    // Wrong case
const max_retries = 3;                      // Wrong case
function CalculateTotal() {}                // Wrong case
```

## Architecture Patterns

### Shared Types (REQUIRED)
```typescript
// All types in src/shared/types.ts
// Used by BOTH main and renderer processes
export interface SearchQuery {
  readonly query: string;
  readonly aiProvider: AIProvider;
}
```

### Error Handling (REQUIRED EVERYWHERE)
```typescript
// ✅ ALWAYS include try-catch for async operations
try {
  setLoadingState(LoadingState.PROCESSING);
  const result = await searchFiles(query);
  setSearchResult(result);
} catch (error) {
  const message = error instanceof Error ? error.message : 'Unknown error';
  setError({ type: ErrorType.SEARCH_ERROR, message, timestamp: new Date() });
} finally {
  setLoadingState(LoadingState.IDLE);
}
```

### Loading States (REQUIRED for UI)
```typescript
// ✅ ALWAYS manage loading states
const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState<boolean>(false);
const [error, setError] = useState<AppError | null>(null);
const [data, setData] = useState<SearchResult | null>(null);
```

## Frontend-Backend Integration

### IPC Communication Pattern
```typescript
// Main Process (src/main/ipc-handlers.ts)
ipcMain.handle('search:files', async (_, query: SearchQuery) => {
  try {
    const result = await searchEngine.search(query);
    return { success: true, data: result };
  } catch (error) {
    return { success: false, error: error.message };
  }
});

// Renderer Process (src/renderer/hooks/useSearch.ts)
const result = await window.electronAPI.search.searchFiles(query);
```

### State Management with Zustand
```typescript
// ✅ Immutable state updates
set({ searchResult: result, error: null });

// ❌ Never mutate state directly
state.searchResult = result; // WRONG
```

## File Organization

```
src/
├── main/              # Electron Main Process
│   ├── main.ts        # Entry point
│   ├── ipc-handlers.ts # IPC communication
│   └── config-manager.ts
├── renderer/          # React UI
│   ├── components/    # React components
│   ├── hooks/         # Custom hooks
│   └── store/         # Zustand state
├── services/          # Business logic
│   ├── ai-providers/  # AI integrations
│   ├── file-search/   # File search engine
│   └── indexing/      # File indexer
└── shared/            # Shared types/constants
    ├── types.ts       # TypeScript interfaces
    └── constants.ts   # App-wide constants
```

## Code Quality Checklist

Before suggesting ANY code, verify:

### ✅ Type Safety
- [ ] No `any` types
- [ ] Explicit return types
- [ ] Proper null/undefined handling
- [ ] Readonly where applicable

### ✅ Error Handling
- [ ] Try-catch for async operations
- [ ] Error states in UI
- [ ] User-friendly error messages
- [ ] Proper error logging

### ✅ Documentation
- [ ] JSDoc for exported functions
- [ ] Inline comments for complex logic
- [ ] README updated if needed

### ✅ Naming & Structure
- [ ] Correct naming convention
- [ ] Single Responsibility Principle
- [ ] DRY - no code duplication
- [ ] Proper file location

### ✅ Security
- [ ] Input validation
- [ ] No secrets in code
- [ ] Safe IPC communication
- [ ] XSS/injection prevention

### ✅ Performance
- [ ] No unnecessary re-renders
- [ ] Efficient algorithms
- [ ] Lazy loading where appropriate

## Common Patterns

### React Component Pattern
```typescript
/**
 * Component description
 */
interface ComponentProps {
  readonly title: string;
  readonly onSubmit: (value: string) => Promise<void>;
}

export function Component({ title, onSubmit }: ComponentProps): JSX.Element {
  const [value, setValue] = useState<string>('');
  const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState<boolean>(false);
  const [error, setError] = useState<string | null>(null);

  const handleSubmit = useCallback(async (): Promise<void> => {
    try {
      setIsLoading(true);
      setError(null);
      await onSubmit(value);
    } catch (err) {
      setError(err instanceof Error ? err.message : 'Unknown error');
    } finally {
      setIsLoading(false);
    }
  }, [value, onSubmit]);

  return (
    <div>
      {/* JSX */}
    </div>
  );
}
```

### Service Class Pattern
```typescript
/**
 * Service description
 */
export class ServiceName {
  private readonly config: ServiceConfig;

  constructor(config: ServiceConfig) {
    this.config = config;
  }

  /**
   * Method description
   */
  public async execute(input: string): Promise<Result> {
    try {
      this.validate(input);
      return await this.process(input);
    } catch (error) {
      return this.handleError(error);
    }
  }

  private validate(input: string): void {
    if (!input) throw new Error('Input required');
  }

  private async process(input: string): Promise<Result> {
    // implementation
  }

  private handleError(error: unknown): Result {
    // error handling
  }
}
```

## AI Provider Integration

### Always Include
1. **Validation** - Check API keys before use
2. **Availability Check** - Test if provider is reachable
3. **Fallback Logic** - Switch to alternative provider on failure
4. **Error Messages** - User-friendly error messages

### Pattern
```typescript
public async isAvailable(): Promise<boolean> {
  try {
    // Test connection
    await this.testConnection();
    return true;
  } catch (error) {
    return false;
  }
}
```

## Security Rules

### Input Validation (EVERYWHERE)
```typescript
// ✅ Validate all user input
if (!query || query.trim().length === 0) {
  throw new Error('Query cannot be empty');
}

// ✅ Sanitize file paths
const safePath = path.normalize(userPath);
```

### Environment Variables
```typescript
// ✅ Use environment variables for secrets
const apiKey = process.env.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY;

// ❌ NEVER hardcode secrets
const apiKey = "sk-ant-..."; // WRONG!
```

## Testing Approach

When suggesting code changes:
1. Explain what will change
2. Show the full context (not just snippets)
3. Verify it integrates with existing code
4. Consider edge cases
5. Include error scenarios

